analysis:
Unit is a new test-only file provider-swift/Tests/DarkbloomFanHelperTests/FanStartupDiscoveryTests.swift (lines 1-399). It exercises fan helper (TB-010; A-014; T-044..T-048) startup sensor rediscovery. Behaviors tested include:
- implausible temperature -> unsupported mode with no writes (L11-31);
- periodic 30s rediscovery retries that never exhaust (L118-139);
- hot recovery that revokes old leases and requires a fresh renewal before manual mode (L162-193);
- failed Auto restore that retains the journal and blocks discovery (L195-219, T-046);
- sleep/wake, disable and shutdown fencing suspended recovery (L344-394, T-047);
- thermal safetyOverride retained (L257-271, T-048);
- refusal of foreign F0Md/Ftst ownership (L273-289);
- journal written before the first manual write (L112, L185).

No production source is in this unit, so these properties are claims, not verified behavior. The integration pass should check the corresponding DarkbloomFanHelper daemon source changes. Points to examine there:
- rediscovery replaces the controller atomically;
- all leases are invalidated on recovery;
- an in-flight engage cannot survive recovery;
- the retry cadence is bounded;
- sleep/disable/shutdown fence rediscovery, and only wake re-arms it.

One observation: L61 prints an encoded status in tests only, with no secrets. No security regression is identified from the test file alone.
